WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
A small bakery wants a new oven.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.320
A car maker wants a new factory line.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.160
Neither can pay for it
from this week's takings.

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.000
Both need to borrow.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.980
And borrowing has a price:

6
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.340
an interest rate, paid year after year.

7
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.330
So where does the money
businesses borrow come from,

8
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.430
and what decides its price?

9
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.310
In this mission, you'll build a
market where borrowers meet lenders,

10
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.620
with its own supply and demand.

11
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.630
Then you'll run a graph lab:

12
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.730
the government starts borrowing more,

13
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.510
and you predict what
happens to everyone else.

14
00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.970
Your mission: find out who lends,

15
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.610
who borrows, and what sets the price.
